back, it was predicted that quantum confinement for the charge carriers is responsible to enhance the thermoelec- tric efficiency. In such situations, half Huesler alloys alongside with skutterudites, clathrates, and silicides were used in practice to tackle the problems. The short- comings of poor durability at high temperatures and low

abundance found in such materials are incapable in wide commercialization purposes. Thermoelectric oxide mate- rials in this regard are considered to encounter these dif- ficulties, which are prominent incompetence sources. The conversion ability of thermoelectric material depends upon ZT known as figure of merit and is enumerated by

\begin{equation}
Z T=\frac{S^{2}\sigma}{\kappa_{\mathrm{e l e c t r o n i c}}+\kappa_{\mathrm{l a t t i c e}}}T.
\end{equation}

