occupation of κL. Howsoever, another part electronic thermal conductivity rises with the rise in temperature. The calculated values at 0 K and 0 GPa of γ are 2.35, 3.20 and 4.9 for Co2XAl (X = Zr, Nb, Hf), respectively consis- tent to intended κL of 7.3, 3.07 and 2.55 W/mK, respec- tively. Hence, due to high anharmonicity displaying that these Heuslers deliver high and low thermal conductivity for Co2XAl (X = Zr, Nb, Hf) with the variation of the temperature.

